														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-3869351">
									

<p>Eh. This one fell a little flat for me, I'm afraid.</p>
<p>The idea of an instrument, that when played allows a user to rewrite reality is an interesting one, but as a reader, I don't feel you really explore the concept enough, just a before and after glimpse that leaves me feeling like there is a particularly large hole in your narrative, as well as missing pieces as to the true power and potential of this artifact. You don't build up to a grand ending so much as you go straight from the piolet episode to the series finale.</p>
<p>Additionally, as a contest entry, the tie into the History theme seems tangential at best, since you don't really dive deep enough into the implications of wholesale rewriting history outside of a few cursory name and format changes.</p>
<p>-1. Solid idea, but the execution could use some work.</p>

